*** Add File:docs/robotics/README.md
+# Robotics & AV extension for Aegis
+
+This folder provides example integrations and stubs to bring Aegis into robotics and autonomous vehicle workflows:
+
+- Triton inference Helm chart (robots/triton): run Triton on GPU nodes for low-latency inference with model repository mounting.
+- ROS2 bridge (robots/ros2_bridge): minimal ROS2 node that forwards sensor metadata/payloads to Aegis ingestion endpoint; in production prefer object-store pointers for large frames.
+- CARLA simulation orchestrator (robots/simulation): run scenarios and store logs for evidence.
+- Evidence pack collector (robots/safety/evidence_pack.py): collects MCP, SLSA attestations, and sim logs into a zip for compliance.
+- Watchdog sidecar & OPA policy examples: runtime assurance patterns to trigger safe-stop.
+- OTA signing helper (ota/ota_sign_and_deploy.sh) using cosign.
+- Adversarial test harness (adversarial/adversarial_test.py) to run FGSM-style perturbation tests as part of CI.
+
+Caveats:
+- These are examples and scaffolds. Safety-critical systems require extensive engineering, formal verification, HIL testing, and compliance work.
+- For high-throughput sensor data, use Kafka/NATS + object-store pointers (LakeFS). Avoid sending full frames in HTTP bodies in production.
+
